      "text": "Flight to Mendoza and a tour of the city"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4b5ff9b4a37f43cc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "6d9b9eadca6e048fbbb977c839bf1c3338b9627b18e738e768d55972c3ecc9ca",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-wm-p7lxhnqwgwc",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, transfer to the airport for your flight to Mendoza.\n\nOn arrival, you'll be met and taken to your hotel for a short rest.\n\nThen set out on a sightseeing tour of Mendoza, which lasts about three hours.\n\nThe city was founded in the 16th century and was initially governed from Chile. A major earthquake in the 19th century destroyed much of the old city. The ruins of the Church of San Francisco are among the surviving traces of early Mendoza you'll learn about on the tour.\n\nToday, Mendoza has more than 100,000 residents. Despite the dry climate, the city is remarkably green, with about 80,000 trees and an extensive network of canals.\n\nOn the tour, you'll see Plaza España, Plaza Independencia, San Martín Park and Cerro de la Gloria, with its statue of José de San Martín.\n\nThe hill offers a panoramic view of the city."
    },
